> I looked at the code.  What exactly should we be looked for.  Certainly it looks like BASIC code.  Since Bally BASIC has unprintable characters (multiply,divide), how do you handle that?

I just typed in the table found at Bally Basic Manual appendix A (page 98), with the following changes:

GO is a line feed, of course;
SPACE is a " ", too;
The arrows were changed for <-, ^, ->, v;
Multiply is a lowercase x;
(Most) commands in a single character were added a trailing space to improve reading;
At the end of the file I found a 255 ($FF) character, so I changed it to <EOF>.

But it is just a test, it is not intended for "archiving" :)


